{
  "rule": "spherical_laplacian_nonuniform",
  "metric": "Linf",
  "expected_min_order": 1.9,
  "notes": "Conservative non-uniform spherical Laplacian r^{-2}*Dr(r^2*Dr(u)). Face fluxes F_{i+1/2} = r_{i+1/2}^2 * (u[i+1]-u[i]) / dr[i+1] and F_{i-1/2} = r_{i-1/2}^2 * (u[i]-u[i-1]) / dr[i] with r_{i+1/2} = 0.5*(r[i]+r[i+1]); divergence = 2*(F_{i+1/2}-F_{i-1/2}) / (r[i]^2*(dr[i]+dr[i+1])). Reduces to spherical_laplacian_uniform when dr is constant. O(dr^2) theory; require observed min order >= 1.9 on geometrically-stretched grids."
}
